  {
   "id": "e07J8srLBgAJ",
   "from": "David Bernasconi",
   "author": "c6847fe2e1ee86d3",
   "date": "2019-11-18T17:29:00Z",
   "subject": "Re: [oscr] sessions within sessions",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks a bunch Chris this is super helpful. Is it also possible to do the opposite and split sessions  to get sub-session estimates? In my case, each one of my  24 sessions is comprised of  a group of 6 detector grids spread across my study site. I currently have the grid names listed as a tdf covariate &quot;site&quot; but that of course will not allow me to get density. In that case, how do I get grid specific density estimates within a session?<div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div><br></div><div>David</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>On Monday, November 18, 2019 at 9:37:18 AM UTC-5, Chris Sutherland wrote:</div></div>"
    ],
    [
